{"type":"standard","title":"Sanie language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Sanie language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q7418287","titles":{"canonical":"Sanie_language","normalized":"Sanie language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Sanie language</span></span>"},"pageid":37043965,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1330691930","tid":"172d2409-e766-11f0-a4fa-389ca487e5a8","timestamp":"2026-01-01T23:03:31Z","description":"Loloish language spoken in China","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanie_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanie_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanie_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Sanie_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanie_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Sanie_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanie_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Sanie_language"}},"extract":"Sanie is a Loloish language of Yunnan, China. It is similar to Samataw. There were 17,320 ethnic Sanie in 1998, but only about 8,000 spoke the Sanie language fluently. The Sanie are also known as the White Yi (白彝).","extract_html":"<p><b>Sanie</b> is a Loloish language of Yunnan, China. It is similar to Samataw. There were 17,320 ethnic Sanie in 1998, but only about 8,000 spoke the Sanie language fluently. The Sanie are also known as the <i>White Yi</i> (白彝).</p>"}